    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72227" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀϊζ-ύς</span></b> , Trag. and later 
			Ion.
		 (<i><span class="en">
			Herod.
			7.39
		</span></i>) <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰζύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ύος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>woe, misery,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόνος καὶ ὀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.2
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάματος καὶ ὀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.365
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				177
			</span></i>: 
				contr.
			 dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀϊζυῖ</span> for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀϊζύϊ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				7.270
			</span></i> : acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀϊζύα</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀϊζύν</span> first in <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				2.88
			</span></i>: Trag. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰζύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					756
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eu.</u>
				893
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				949
			</span></i>(lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as pr.
			n., daughter of Night, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				214
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span> in nom. and
			acc., v.
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
			</span></i> l. c. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ</span> in other
			cases.]</div>
